8. SHIPMENT CANCELLATION RULES

Improve the cancellation system.

I want customers to be able to cancel a shipment only while cancellation is operationally possible.

My preferred business rule is:

Once a shipment has left Swiftvero’s custody and has been handed over to the shipping carrier, it cannot be cancelled through the normal customer cancellation process.

Implement clear cancellation stages.

STAGE A: BEFORE PICKUP

If the customer has booked a pickup but the package has not yet been collected:

* Allow cancellation.
* Allow cancellation of Standard Pickup.
* Allow cancellation of Priority Pickup.
* Apply any clearly disclosed priority pickup fee refund rules.
* Record the cancellation reason.
* Notify the relevant staff.

STAGE B: PACKAGE COLLECTED BUT NOT YET HANDED OVER TO THE SHIPPING CARRIER

If the package has been collected or has arrived at the Swiftvero facility but has not yet been handed over to the shipping carrier:

* Do not automatically treat the shipment as non-cancellable.
* Allow a cancellation request for review.
* Check whether the package has already been packed, processed or prepared for shipping.
* Apply any disclosed handling or return charges where applicable.
* Allow authorised staff to approve or reject the request.
* Explain any applicable refund or return conditions.

STAGE C: HANDED OVER TO THE SHIPPING CARRIER

Once the package has been handed over to the shipping carrier or has left Swiftvero’s custody:

* Disable the normal cancellation button.
* Clearly display that the shipment can no longer be cancelled.
* Allow the customer to contact support for assistance.
* Explain that any available return or interception request depends on the carrier and applicable service terms.
* Do not promise that a return or interception is possible.

STAGE D: DELIVERED

A delivered shipment cannot be cancelled.

Any complaint must go through the support, claims or refund process where applicable.

CANCELLATION POLICY

Keep the detailed cancellation policy under:

Policies → Cancellation and Refund Policy

Do not display long cancellation explanations during every booking step.

Show a short relevant summary before confirmation.

Make the full policy available to customers whenever they want to read it.

IMPORTANT TECHNICAL RULE

The cancellation restriction must be enforced by the backend.

Do not rely only on hiding the cancellation button.

Staff permissions and shipment status must prevent unauthorised cancellation after the carrier handover stage.

Record all cancellation requests, approvals, rejections and refunds in the audit history.

