FINAL PRODUCT DIRECTION

Swiftvero must feel like a premium international logistics platform, not a collection of unrelated dashboards.

The individual customer should feel that the service is simple and personal.

The business customer should feel that the platform understands business shipping and provides the tools needed to manage shipments.

The guest should be able to get a quote, book a supported pickup, track a shipment and contact support without unnecessary barriers.

The staff should have the information and controls needed to manage real operations.

The customer should always understand:

* What is happening to their package.
* Where their package was last confirmed.
* What happens next.
* What they need to pay.
* What they can cancel.
* What money they can get back.
* How to contact Swiftvero.

Keep the website clean. Put detailed policies in the Policy Centre. Put notification preferences in Settings. Keep the notification bell for notifications only. Keep tracking clear and useful. Keep the wallet transparent and secure.

Do not sacrifice actual business accuracy just to make the interface look attractive.

Build the platform as though it will serve real individual customers, established businesses and international shipping operations every day.